Still only planned is an X86 HGX Rubin NVL 8, 8 Rubin GPUs on NV link, 264 core Intel

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:18.360
Zeon 6 CPUs, 4 terabytes of DDR5, and 6.4 terabytes per second of RDMA networking.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.360
Tom's hardware calls the standalone Vera instances and vidia's first CPU push of this kind

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:30.540
at a hyperscaler, beside OCI's existing Ampere Ultra-Arm option. Nvidia has put

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:38.820
Vera memory bandwidth at 1.2 terabytes per second on LPDDR5 X9,600. In a stream triad test,

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:47.400
Tom's hardware ran off OCI. That box more than doubled a dual Intel Xeon 6,980P server on MRDIMs

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:53.960
at 8800 Megatransfer's per second. In Abelene, OpenAI has already trained and served on an OCI

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:58.140
supercluster with more than 100,000 Blackwell GPUs.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.120
Google Cloud announced VeraRubin General Availability last week.

00:02:03.152 --> 00:02:09.652
SK Heinex's third quarter, reported by EE Times, brought revenue of 104.62 trillion

00:02:09.652 --> 00:02:11.672
won, about $78 billion.

00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:19.852
Operating profit was 83.33 trillion won, about $62 billion at an 80% operating margin.

00:02:19.852 --> 00:02:27.992
Net profit was 39.78 trillion won, about 30 billion dollars, and net cash rose to 98.7 trillion

00:02:27.992 --> 00:02:35.112
won, about 74 billion dollars. Counterpoints MS Huang said that profit beat a 77 trillion

00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:42.192
won consensus, about 57 billion dollars. He said standard DRAM has moved from 20 to 30 cents per

00:02:42.192 --> 00:02:49.512
gigabit to $2 per gigabit, and put the global DRAM market at 200 billion dollars. He argued HBM

00:02:49.512 --> 00:02:55.372
PM4 could reach $4 per gigabit, and said October has cleared fears that SK Heinix could

00:02:55.372 --> 00:03:00.412
not ship HBM4 to Nvidia, or that HBM attached per chip would shrink.

00:03:01.052 --> 00:03:05.772
Tech PowerUp says average selling prices rose more than 20% from the prior quarter.

00:03:06.412 --> 00:03:11.312
Digitimes reports the company saying customers want more than twice the HBM it can supply.

00:03:12.072 --> 00:03:16.472
Korea Junyang Daily reports DRAM and HBM booked through 2029.

00:03:16.472 --> 00:03:22.612
The company expects demand to outrun supply through 2030, pointing at 10 nanometer-class

00:03:22.612 --> 00:03:26.232
6th generation DRAM and 321 layer NAND.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:32.432
Long-term agreements with 14 tech giants cover more than half of capacity for 2027 and

00:03:32.432 --> 00:03:33.212
2028.

00:03:33.892 --> 00:03:39.052
Counterpoint expects Samsung to lead HBM share from HBM 4 in 2027.

00:03:39.812 --> 00:03:43.352
SK Heinrich says its packaging and customer ties will hold the lead.

00:03:44.565 --> 00:03:50.245
CXMT in a Reuters report carried by tech power-up is expected to start mass production of its

00:03:50.245 --> 00:03:58.065
first HBM, HBM3E within two months by the end of 2026. Risk production started in August

00:03:58.065 --> 00:04:03.325
and yields are still the problem. The outlet says it lacks CXMT's own speed numbers

00:04:03.325 --> 00:04:12.665
and quotes the JDEC HBM3E envelope, a 1,024-bit bus 9.2-12.4 gigabits per second per pin.

00:04:12.665 --> 00:04:20.265
Most configs at 9.6, about 1.2 terabytes per second, 24 gigabytes in an 8 high stack

00:04:20.265 --> 00:04:27.325
or 36 in a 12 high of 24 gigabit layers. Front-end yield is put around 30%, with back-end

00:04:27.325 --> 00:04:34.885
processing adding about 70% on top of that 30%. The same report says CXMT is trying HBM3E

00:04:34.885 --> 00:04:41.925
with about 3,000 through Silicon Via's Perlayer, versus about 5,000 Samsung has used Perlayer on

00:04:41.925 --> 00:04:49.925
HBM2, and more than 8,000 SK Heinix has used on HBM3 in an 8-high stack and is unlikely to reach

00:04:49.925 --> 00:04:57.275
12 high soon. Intel Chief Lip Bhutan at a October 24 chat with Jimmy Chang of the Chinese-American

00:04:57.275 --> 00:05:03.275
Semiconductor Professional Association said he has talked with AMD Chief Lisa Su about possible

00:05:03.275 --> 00:05:09.915
cooperation. Tech PowerUp says he named no area and neither company has announced a deal. AMD

00:05:09.915 --> 00:05:17.055
was earlier reported to be looking at Intel's 14A node. 18A is in volume production. 14A has

00:05:17.055 --> 00:05:25.015
its 0.5 process design kit out. 0.9 is next and 1.0 is aimed at volume production early next year.

00:05:25.655 --> 00:05:29.555
October was the target for handing the 0.9 kit to outside customers.

00:05:29.555 --> 00:05:34.075
10 state-tuned line is read as meaning that handoff has not happened.

00:05:34.575 --> 00:05:40.535
He said Intel must take back CPU leadership and will tailor parts such as Xeon to what customers ask for.

00:05:41.175 --> 00:05:45.795
He named ASICs, co-packaged optics, physical AI, and advanced packaging,

00:05:46.375 --> 00:05:50.355
and wants two or three of those to reach about 10% of Intel revenue each.

00:05:51.373 --> 00:05:55.893
Nebula says it will deploy more than 1000 Blackwell Ultra GPUs in Belgium.

00:05:56.513 --> 00:06:01.473
TechSign Global has that as a deployment plan, with no site power figure attached.

00:06:02.013 --> 00:06:07.873
US Signal has bought a data center in Hillsboro, Oregon that Oracle previously occupied data

00:06:07.873 --> 00:06:09.213
center dynamics reports.

00:06:09.853 --> 00:06:11.833
